  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Jesus Children Of America** (1 other source): Jesus Children Of America opens, moves into Who Knows, then returns to Jesus Children Of America [1]\n- **Lenny** (1 other source): Lenny flows directly into Turn It Out without a break [1]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Let The Music Take Your Mind**: back after 74 archived shows (493 days); rare: 3 archived performances [2]\n- **Romantic**: rare: 7 archived performances [2]\n- **The World Is A Ghetto**: rare: 14 archived performances [2]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **soulive2001-07-01.shnf** (recommended): matrix (soundboard mixed with audience mics); 13 songs; 169 min [1]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Deantoni Parks, James Hurt and Brian Jordan sat in for the closing songs, The World Is A Ghetto and One In Seven [1]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **soulive2001-07-01.shnf**: taped by Pete Costello; transferred by Kurt Ruthe; source: schoeps CmC6 (onstage) + dsbd matrix > ? > DAT [1]",
